## Examples and Runnable Demos Policy

**Policy summary**
- Text and reference docs: edit files in this repo.
- Runnable demos: host on an approved sandbox and add the demo to `examples/manifest.json`.
- Do not paste full runnable example code into markdown files. Embeds or short summaries only.

**Approved demo hosts**
- codesandbox.io
- jsfiddle.net
- dabblet.com
- self-hosted sandboxes listed in this repo (your-self-hosted-domain.example)

**How to add or update a demo**
1. Create or update the demo on an approved host.
2. Add or update an entry in `examples/manifest.json` with `id`, `title`, `canonical_url`, `description`, `tags`, and `authors`.
3. In the doc, embed the demo or include a short summary and link to the canonical URL.
4. Open a PR. CI will validate the manifest and block PRs that paste full example code.

**PR checklist**
- [ ] I updated the canonical demo on an approved host or updated `examples/manifest.json`.
- [ ] I did not paste full runnable code into the doc.
- [ ] I added authorship metadata to the manifest entry.
